#. type: SH
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid "archinstall - archinstall Documentation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"B<archinstall> is library which can be used to install Arch Linux.  The "
"library comes packaged with different pre-configured installers, such as the "
"default I<\\%Guided installation> installer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"A demo of the I<\\%Guided installation> installer can be seen here: \\X'tty: "
"link https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9Xt7X_Iqg6E'I<\\%https://"
"www.youtube.com/watch?v=9Xt7X_Iqg6E>\\X'tty: link'\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid "Some of the features of Archinstall are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\(bu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"B<Context friendly.> The library always executes calls in sequential order "
"to ensure installation-steps don\\(aqt overlap or execute in the wrong "
"order. It also supports I<(and uses)> context wrappers to ensure cleanup and "
"final tasks such as B<mkinitcpio> are called when needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"B<Full transparency> Logs and insights can be found at B</var/log/"
"archinstall> both in the live ISO and partially on the installed system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"B<Accessibility friendly> Archinstall works with B<espeakup> and other "
"accessibility tools thanks to the use of a TUI."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "GUIDED INSTALLATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Archinstall ships with a pre-programmed \\X'tty: link https://github.com/"
"archlinux/archinstall/blob/master/archinstall/scripts/guided.py'I<\\%Guided "
"Installer>\\X'tty: link' guiding you through the mandatory steps as well as "
"some optional configurations that can be done."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid "B<NOTE:>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Other pre-programmed scripts can be invoked by executing B<archinstall "
"E<lt>scriptE<gt>> I<(without .py)>\\&. To see a complete list of scripts, "
"run B<archinstall --script list> or check the source code \\X'tty: link "
"https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/tree/master/archinstall/scripts'I<\\"
"%scripts>\\X'tty: link' directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"It\\(aqs recommended to run B<archinstall> from the official Arch Linux ISO."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid "B<WARNING:>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"The installer will not configure WiFi before the installation begins. You "
"need to read up on \\X'tty: link https://wiki.archlinux.org/index.php/"
"Network_configuration'I<\\%Arch Linux networking>\\X'tty: link' before you "
"continue."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running the guided installation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid "To start the installer, run the following in the latest Arch Linux ISO:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "archinstall\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Since the \\X'tty: link https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/blob/master/"
"archinstall/scripts/guided.py'I<\\%Guided Installer>\\X'tty: link' is the "
"default script, this is the equivalent of running B<archinstall guided>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"The guided installation also supports installing with pre-configured answers "
"to all the guided steps. This can be a quick and convenient way to re-run "
"one or several installations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid "There are two configuration files, both are optional."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "--config"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"This parameter takes a local or remote B<\\&.json> file as argument and "
"contains the overall configuration and menu answers for the guided installer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"You can always get the latest options for this file with B<archinstall --dry-"
"run>, this executes the guided installer in a safe mode where no permanent "
"actions will be taken on your system but simulate a run and save the "
"configuration to disk."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example usage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "archinstall --config https://domain.lan/config.json\n"
msgstr ""

