#. type: SH
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "KNOWN ISSUES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Some issues are out of the \\X'tty: link https://github.com/archlinux/"
"archinstall/'I<\\%archinstall>\\X'tty: link' projects scope, and the ones we "
"know of are listed below."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "Waiting for time sync \\X'tty: link https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/issues/2144'I<\\%#2144>\\X'tty: link'"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"The usual root cause of this is the network topology.  More specifically "
"\\X'tty: link https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/blob/"
"e6344f93f7e476d05bbcd642f2ed91fdde545870/archinstall/lib/"
"installer.py#L136'I<\\%timedatectl show>\\X'tty: link' cannot perform a "
"proper time sync against the default servers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Restarting B<systemd-timesyncd.service> might work but most often you need "
"to configure B</etc/systemd/timesyncd.conf> to match your network design."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"If you know your time is correct on the machine, you can run B<archinstall --"
"skip-ntp> to ignore time sync."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "Missing Nvidia Proprietary Driver \\X'tty: link https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/issues/2002'I<\\%#2002>\\X'tty: link'"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"In some instances, the nvidia driver might not have all the necessary "
"packages installed.  This is due to the kernel selection and/or hardware "
"setups requiring additional packages to work properly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"A common workaround is to install the package \\X'tty: link https://"
"archlinux.org/packages/core/x86_64/linux-headers/'I<\\%linux-"
"headers>\\X'tty: link' and \\X'tty: link https://archlinux.org/packages/"
"extra/x86_64/nvidia-dkms/'I<\\%nvidia-dkms>\\X'tty: link'"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "ARM, 32bit and other CPU types error out \\X'tty: link https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/issues/1686'I<\\%#1686>\\X'tty: link', \\X'tty: link https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/issues/2185'I<\\%#2185>\\X'tty: link'"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"This is a bit of a catch-all known issue.  Officially \\X'tty: link https://"
"wiki.archlinux.org/title/"
"Frequently_asked_questions#What_architectures_does_Arch_support?'I<\\"
"%x86_64>\\X'tty: link' is only supported by Arch Linux.  Hence little effort "
"have been put into supporting other platforms."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"In theory, other architectures should work but small quirks might arise."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"PR\\(aqs are welcome but please be respectful of the delays in merging.  "
"Other fixes, issues or features will be prioritized for the above reasons."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keyring is out of date \\X'tty: link https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/issues/2213'I<\\%#2213>\\X'tty: link'"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Missing key-issues tend to be that the \\X'tty: link https://archlinux.org/"
"packages/core/any/archlinux-keyring/'I<\\%archlinux-keyring>\\X'tty: link' "
"package is out of date, usually as a result of an outdated ISO.  There is an "
"attempt from upstream to fix this issue, and it\\(aqs the \\X'tty: link "
"https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/archlinux-keyring/-/blob/"
"7e672dad10652a80d1cc575d75cdb46442cd7f96/wkd_sync/archlinux-keyring-wkd-"
"sync.service.in'I<\\%archlinux-keyring-wkd-sync.service>\\X'tty: link'"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"The service starts almost immediately during boot, and if network is not "
"configured in time — the service will fail.  Subsequently the B<archinstall> "
"run might operate on a old keyring despite there being an update service for "
"this."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"There is really no way to reliably over time work around this issue in "
"B<archinstall>\\&.  Instead, efforts to the upstream service should be "
"considered the way forward. And/or keys not expiring between a sane amount "
"of ISO\\(aqs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"The issue can happen on new ISO\\(aqs too even as little as a few days after "
"release, as some keys might expire right after the keyring is I<\"burnt "
"in\"> to the ISO."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Another common issue relating to the network not being configured, is that "
"time might not be set correctly - resulting in the keyring not being able to "
"update. See I<\\%Waiting for time sync #2144>\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "AUR packages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"This is also a catch-all issue.  \\X'tty: link https://wiki.archlinux.org/"
"title/Arch_User_Repository#Updating_packages'I<\\%AUR is "
"unsupported>\\X'tty: link', and until that changes we cannot use AUR "
"packages to solve feature requests in B<archinstall>\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"This means that feature requests like supporting filesystems such as "
"\\X'tty: link https://aur.archlinux.org/packages/zfs-linux'I<\\%ZFS>\\X'tty: "
"link' can not be added, and issues cannot be solved by using AUR packages "
"either."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"But in spirit of giving the community options, B<archinstall> supports I<\\"
"%Python Plugins>, which means you can run B<archinstall --plugin "
"E<lt>urlE<gt>> and source an AUR plugin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"\\X'tty: link https://github.com/torxed/archinstall-aur'I<\\%torxed/"
"archinstall-aur>\\X'tty: link' is a reference implementation for plugins:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "# archinstall --plugin https://archlinux.life/aur-plugin\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"\\X'tty: link https://github.com/phisch/archinstall-aur'I<\\%phisch/"
"archinstall-aur>\\X'tty: link' is another alternative:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "# archinstall --plugin https://raw.githubusercontent.com/phisch/archinstall-aur/master/archinstall-aur.py\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid "This will allow for unsupported usage of AUR during installation."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "REPORT ISSUES & BUGS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Issues and bugs should be reported over at \\X'tty: link https://github.com/"
"archlinux/archinstall/issues'I<\\%https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/"
"issues>\\X'tty: link'\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"General questions, enhancements and security issues can be reported over "
"there too.  For quick issues or if you need help, head over to the Discord "
"server which has a help channel."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "Log files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"When submitting a help ticket, please include the B</var/log/archinstall/"
"install.log>\\&.  It can be found both on the live ISO but also in the "
"installed filesystem if the base packages were strapped in."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid "B<TIP:>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An easy way to submit logs is B<curl -F\\(aqfile=@/var/log/archinstall/install.log\\(aq https://0x0.st>\\&.\n"
"Use caution when submitting other log files, but B<archinstall> pledges to keep B<install.log> safe for posting publicly!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"There are additional log files under B</var/log/archinstall/> that can be "
"useful:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"B</var/log/archinstall/user_configuration.json> - Stores most of the guided "
"answers in the installer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"B</var/log/archinstall/user_credentials.json> - Stores any usernames or "
"passwords, can be passed to B<--creds>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"B</var/log/archinstall/user_disk_layouts.json> - Stores the chosen disks and "
"their layouts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"B</var/log/archinstall/install.log> - A log file over what steps were taken "
"by archinstall"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"B</var/log/archinstall/cmd_history.txt> - A complete command history, "
"command by command in order"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"B</var/log/archinstall/cmd_output.txt> - A raw output from all the commands "
"that were executed by archinstall"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"We only try to guarantee that B</var/log/archinstall/install.log> is free "
"from sensitive information.  Any other log file should be pasted with "
"B<utmost care>!"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "DISCORD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"There\\(aqs a discord channel which is frequented by some \\X'tty: link "
"https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/graphs/contributors'I<\\"
"%contributors>\\X'tty: link'\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"To join the server, head over to \\X'tty: link https://discord.gg/"
"aDeMffrxNg'I<\\%https://discord.gg/aDeMffrxNg>\\X'tty: link' and join in.  "
"There\\(aqs not many rules other than common sense and to treat others with "
"respect. The general chat is for off-topic things as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"There\\(aqs the B<@Party Animals> role if you want notifications of new "
