"the B<@Contributors> role can be activated by contributors by writing B<!"
"verify> and follow the verification process."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid "Hop in, we hope to see you there! : )"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "PYTHON LIBRARY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Archinstall ships on \\X'tty: link https://pypi.org/'I<\\%PyPi>\\X'tty: "
"link' as I<\\%archinstall>\\&.  But the library can be installed manually as "
"well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"These steps are not required if you want to use archinstall on the official "
"Arch Linux ISO."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "Installing with pacman"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Archinstall is on the \\X'tty: link https://wiki.archlinux.org/index.php/"
"Official_repositories'I<\\%official repositories>\\X'tty: link'\\&.  And it "
"will also install archinstall as a python library."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid "To install both the library and the archinstall script:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "pacman -S archinstall\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can install only the library and not the helper "
"executable using the B<python-archinstall> package."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "Installing from PyPI"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid "The basic concept of PyPI applies using I<pip>\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "pip install archinstall\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install using source code"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"You can also install using the source code.  For sake of simplicity we will "
"use B<git clone> in this example."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "git clone https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid "You can either move the folder into your project and simply do"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "import archinstall\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Or you can PyPa\\(aqs \\X'tty: link https://github.com/pypa/build'I<\\"
"%build>\\X'tty: link' and \\X'tty: link https://github.com/pypa/"
"installer'I<\\%installer>\\X'tty: link' to install it into pythons module "
"path."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ cd archinstall\n"
"$ python -m build .\n"
"$ python -m installer dist/*.whl\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "PYTHON MODULE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Archinstall supports running in \\X'tty: link https://docs.python.org/3/"
"library/__main__.html'I<\\%module mode>\\X'tty: link'\\&.  The way the "
"library is invoked in module mode is limited to executing scripts under the "
"\\X'tty: link https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/tree/master/"
"archinstall/scripts'I<\\%scripts>\\X'tty: link' folder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"It\\(aqs therefore important to place any script or profile you wish to "
"invoke in the examples folder prior to building and installing."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pre-requisites"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"We\\(aqll assume you\\(aqve followed the I<\\%Install using source code> "
"method.  Before actually installing the library, you will need to place your "
"custom installer-scripts under \\X'tty: link https://github.com/archlinux/"
"archinstall/tree/master/archinstall/scripts'I<\\%scripts>\\X'tty: link' as a "
"python file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid "More on how you create these in the next section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"This is subject to change in the future as this method is currently a bit "
"stiff. The script path will become a parameter. But for now, this is by "
"design."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "Creating a script"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Lets create a I<test_installer> - installer as an example. This is assuming "
"that the folder I<\\&./archinstall> is a git-clone of the main repo.  We "
"begin by creating \"\\X'tty: link https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/"
"tree/master/archinstall/scripts'I<\\%scripts>\\X'tty: link'B</"
"test_installer.py>\". The placement here is important later."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"This script can now already be called using B<python -m archinstall "
"test_installer> after a successful installation of the library itself.  But "
"the script won\\(aqt do much. So we\\(aqll do something simple like list all "
"the hard drives as an example."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"To do this, we\\(aqll begin by importing B<archinstall> in our \"\\X'tty: "
"link https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/tree/master/archinstall/"
"scripts'I<\\%scripts>\\X'tty: link'B</test_installer.py>\" and call a "
"function whtin B<archinstall>\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "print(archinstall.disk.device_handler.devices)\n"
msgstr ""

